Patch 0083: chain-mode DMA reuses its gather buffers (PS2Memory::writeIORegister).
What: every chain DMA created a fresh std::vector<uint8_t> and grew it chunk by chunk with insert(); in a 4-player fight that
was ~70% of the game thread's memcpy (~0.8 ms/frame) plus a free/madvise on release. The buffer now comes from a small pool
(acquireChainBuffer(), 64 KiB reserved on first use), is moved into the pending transfer as before, and
processPendingTransfers() hands the buffers back (recycleTransfers(), capacity kept, at most 8 pooled); an empty chain
returns its buffer too. Same bytes, same order, same cycle accounting: only where the memory comes from changes.
Verified: tests/runtime configured against this tree compiles and passes (36 passed).
Original work, GPL-3.0.
